    "long_instructions": "## Modify & Make (The \"Safe\" App)\r\n\r\nNow, we are going to install a \"Safety Net.\" We use `try...catch` blocks to tell the computer: \"Try doing this, but if you hit a snag, don't crash just do this other thing instead.\"\r\n\r\nRewrite your `btn.addEventListener` in `script.js` using `try...catch` blocks. \r\n\r\n_Hint: You will need to wrap the dangerous code inside a `try` block and provide instructions for the failure inside a `catch` block._",
